msgid "AI Agent Abilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3436
msgid "Requires WordPress 6.9 or newer. This site is running an older version, so nothing is registered either way."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3441
msgid "Let AI tools and agents look up translation information"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3444
msgid "Registers four read-only abilities through WordPress's Abilities API: list languages, get a post's translations, detect a post's language, and convert a URL to another language. They respect the calling user's permissions and cost nothing when no agent is installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3448
msgid "Also let them create and machine-translate content"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3451
msgid "Adds two abilities that WRITE: create a translation, and machine-translate a post. Machine translation spends your provider quota, so an agent could use it without you seeing the request. Off by default for that reason - turn it on if you are deliberately automating translation through an agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3456
msgid "Dashboard Widget"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3460
msgid "Show a translation-overview widget on the WordPress Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3463
msgid "Displays active languages and content-translation coverage at a glance. Only shown to users who can manage languages, loads only on the Dashboard screen, and reads cached counts (no extra queries on dashboard load)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3468
msgid "Edge Worker Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3472
msgid "Publish /perflocale/v1/config endpoint and honour X-PerfLocale-Lang hints"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3475
msgid "Exposes a cache-friendly public REST endpoint that a Cloudflare Worker, Vercel Edge function, or Netlify Edge function can read to pre-route visitors to the correct language before the request reaches PHP. Also adds an Edge Hint Redirect method, which you switch on under URL &amp; Routing; with two or more redirect methods enabled you can set the order they run in."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3476
msgid "Restricting access to the endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3480
msgid "Endpoint:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3484
msgid "A reference Worker implementation is included at:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3488
msgid "Note: the endpoint is public (required so edge workers can read it without credentials). Any paths you add to \"Excluded paths\" in URL & Routing will be visible in the JSON payload. If a path is sensitive, route around it instead of relying on it being hidden."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3492
msgid "Leave disabled if you are not running a Cloudflare Worker / Vercel Edge / Netlify Edge function. When off, no REST route is registered and no hint headers are consumed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3498
msgid "CDN Cache-Tag Headers"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3502
msgid "Emit Cache-Tag response headers so CDNs can purge by language or by specific content"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3505
msgid "Adds a Cache-Tag header to every frontend page with tags like lang:bg_BG, post:123, home. Compatible with Cloudflare (Cache-Tag), Bunny (Cache-Tag), and Fastly (rename to Surrogate-Key via filter). Enables surgical purges instead of flushing the entire edge cache on every save."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3506
msgid "CDN setup examples"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3510
msgid "Leave disabled if your hosting does not sit behind a CDN that reads these tags. When off, no send_headers hook is registered."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3516
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Pages/SettingsPage.php:3522
msgid "When enabled, deleting the plugin will remove all translation data, languages, settings, and database tables. When disabled, your data is preserved for reinstallation. This is a one-shot teardown setting - toggle it before deleting the plugin from <em>Plugins → Installed Plugins</em>."
msgstr ""

